        "id": 70087,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-17T17:21:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was trying to make it more of a hunt for what the cultists are doing, I tried to come up with a better way to have heroes find the location of the relics, to locate the summoning, but I couldn't come up with anything better.</p><p>What I tried to accomplish instead is a sense that the heroes are able to prepare themselves somewhat for the confrontation, that they have some control over the situation, in a tug of war style struggle between the cult and heroes.</p><p>I've also found the second side isn't as nasty as the first. &nbsp;The first side is a nasty battle to get set up and survive while the Cultists pound on you. &nbsp;Damage drops off substantially on the second side but I like flooding the pins out and the quick deck play. &nbsp;Flipping Gloomy with several cultists in play can really crush the heroes ability to do anything. &nbsp;I've tried it with the second side Advanced text being reduced damage dealt for having a pin on you, but if you cap it at one it isn't really anything and if you have it be one per pin a good Vast following can crush your whole team.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
